# Action Shift and Never86.ai

Action Shift is the free one-seat, one-store product. Never call it Pulse. Do not add a multi-store view, a roll-up, or Command Center pricing to Action Shift.

Never86.ai, this repo, is the separate multi-unit build for 1 to 5 units, stretching to 9. It has per-unit views and one all-units roll-up. Pricing for extra units stays TBD unless a price is already approved in this repo. Do not invent one. Do not use the Command Center name.

never86d-beta-ctap, never86-action-shift-live, and app.never86.app are read-only. Do not push, branch, comment, redirect, or change DNS for them.

## Flow
1. Operator names 1 to 9 units.
2. One drop: POS exports, invoices, payroll, delivery statements (DoorDash, Uber Eats, Grubhub), CSV, Excel, PDF, or photos. Paste is allowed.
3. Sort each file by type and by unit. Show the sorting summary so a wrong sort can be fixed.
4. Tally board, then daily numbers, then weekly prime cost.
5. At most 3 ranked actions. Each has an owner, a due date (2 days out), an expected outcome, and a label.

The tally opens with a short "How today went" strip. Biggest dollar misses first. Each category tile carries the same kind of one-line note.

## Labels
Verified, Estimated, or Missing. Sample data is marked on the page. The figure itself still uses those three labels.

- Blank, dash, or unreadable is Missing. Never treat a blank as $0.
- A zero that is written on the file stays zero.
- Hours times a wage on the file is Estimated. A labor dollar column is Verified.
- Quantity times price, with no printed extension, is Estimated.
- A category guessed from the item name is Estimated.
- PDF and photos keep a sort slot. Amounts stay Missing until the rows are CSV or Excel.
- Roll up a dollar only when every unit in the view has that figure. Otherwise the roll-up is Missing and names the unit and the file.
- Do not average percents. Percent is summed dollars divided by summed sales.
- Round callouts to whole dollars and whole percents.

## Tally
Categories: food/COGS, beverage, paper/packaging, labor, delivery fees, other.

Week-to-date dollars and percent of week-to-date sales sit side by side. The board updates as each file lands.

Targets are operator-set percents. No default targets. An empty target stays empty. Zero is a real target only after the operator enters it.

Daily callout, per category, per unit, and for all units:

- Dollars over or under = actual spend minus (target percent times that day's sales).
- Show that dollar next to actual spend as a percent of the day's sales.
- Over: "Labor ran $200 over today. That's 40% of sales, and your target is 30%."
- Under: "Food came in $85 under. Nice, that's 27% of sales."
- No target: say so and ask them to set one.
- Missing sales or spend: name the file. Do not guess.

## Truth
- POS is not payout. Delivery payout is not the fee. Commission, marketing, and error charges stay separate. A missing fee is not zero.
- Invoice is not COGS. Food cost and prime cost need a count (beginning plus purchases minus ending) or a food-cost column on the file.
- Prime cost is COGS plus labor, in dollars and as a percent of sales. If either part is Missing, prime cost is Missing.
- An incomplete week stays Open.
- No count, no food cost. Purchases may still show on the food tile as spend, with that note.
- Labor copy asks what kept the role over the plan. Use the role, not a staff name. No theft or skimming claims.
- Do not say a specific operator uses Toast.
- No em dashes in copy. No desk wording. No portal login. No auto-send.
- Human approves the move. The model ranks. It does not send.

## Checks inside the 3 actions
Invoice: same pack, price change. Labor: schedule against the clock. Menu: plate cost, blank ingredient is not free. Statement: review the fee lines. Dollar misses from the tally outrank those checks. Cap the list at 3.
